      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0265" n="art0265">
        <head>AMATEUR ASSOCIATION'S ANNUAL lIANDICAP.</head>
        <p>AMATEUR ASSOCIATION'S ANNUAL lIANDICAP.</p>
        <p>'Some Interesting Results In The</p>
        <p>Final Rounds.</p>
        <p>A large number of bowling enthusiasts flocked to the well-kept green atta,thed to the :91;1's Head Hotel on Saturday afternoon, when fur- ther, and substantial 'progress was made with the annual handicap in connection with the Warrington and District Amateur Bowling Association. The handicap produced an excel- lent entry, some of the best known bowlers in the neighbourhood having put down their names, with the result that much excellent and interesting trundling was witnessed. • The out- standing games in the first round having been polished off, , the second, third and fourth rounds were forthwith proceeded with, and were completed ere a full afternoon's sport was declared closed. The results were as follows :</p>
      </div>
