        <p>GOLBORNE-STREET BAPTIST CHURCH. FLOWER SUNDAY. TO-MORROW, JULY 18th, 1915. Preacher: Rev. H. OGDEN. Morning, 10.45; Evening, 6.30. AFTERNOON, 2.30, FLOWER SERVICE. Chair: Mrs. ,MOORES. Speaker: Miss BESSIE DUTTON. HYMNS BY THE CHILDREN. Soloist, Evening: Miss BATES. COLLECTIONS. FLOWERS FOR HOSPITALS. T. JOHN'S PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH. WILDERSPOOL CAUSEWAY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), JULY 18th, 1915. Morning. 10.45; Evening. 6.30: Preacher: Rev. PETER WOODS (Hea,dingley College. LPeds).</p>
        <p>BAPTIST CHURCH, LATCHFORD. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), JULY 18th, 1f)15, Morning, 10.30; Evening, 6.30: _ Preacher: Rev. E. E. LOVELL, Lymm.</p>
        <p>PRIMITIVE METHODIST ' CHURCH, „, LEGH-STREET. WARRINGTON. 104ORROW (SUNDAY), JULY 18th, 1015. Morning, 10.30; Evening, 6.30: Rev. A. a. CHESSUM. VIIRISTADELP-HIAN MEETING ROOM, BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON.—Free Bible address SUNDAY NEXT, at 6.30 p.m. Subject: " The Destiny of the Earth." Mr. C. MORRIS, Stockport.</p>
        <p>Public Notices.</p>
