        <p>PRIVATE W. FARRINGTON. Wounded.</p>
        <p>bullet entered his left forearm and severed the main artery. He s now in hospital at Ton- bridge, and is progressing favourably. Private Farrington was formerly employed on the gas-plant at Messrs. Joseph Crosfield's, and leaving there soon after the outbreak of war, he joined the "Terriers." He had pre- viously served in the Cheshire Regiment He is 30 years of age, and was educated at St. James' School. He . worshipped at the Emmanuel Church, Bold-street. PRIVATE HARRY BROADHURST. Prominent Ilowley Liberal's Son Shrapnelled In Head. Private Harry Broadhurst, of Cartwright street, is, we are glad to say, making good pro- gress towards recovery in the -Ulster Volunteer Hospital. He was wounded by shrapnel in the head during the famous charge of the 4th South Lancashires, and doctors state that he must also have been gassed. After being operated on at the base he was sent to a hospital in Dublin, and later to his present abode in the North of Ireland. To his parents he has not written for a fortnight. Private Broadhurst, who Is 29 years of age,</p>
